WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.299
A recruiter hands you three resumes and says:

2
00:00:02.531 --> 00:00:04.087
shortlist the best two.

3
00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.620
You wouldn't answer in one breath. You'd read

4
00:00:06.689 --> 00:00:09.569
one, note a score, read the next. Each

5
00:00:09.603 --> 00:00:11.217
step depends on the last.

6
00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.541
An agent works the same way. It's the

7
00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:16.350
tool call from last lesson, inside a loop.

8
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.185
Think: the model reads everything so far and

9
00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:22.099
picks a tool. Act: your code runs it.

10
00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:25.570
Observe: the result joins the conversation.

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.358
Then round again. List the files. Read a

12
00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:31.679
resume. Save a score. Every lap, the message

13
00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:32.747
list grows.

14
00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:35.256
When the model replies with plain text and

15
00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:37.729
no tool call, that's the final answer, and

16
00:00:37.776 --> 00:00:39.320
the loop ends.

17
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.516
But a stuck model can repeat the same

18
00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:44.894
call forever, and every lap costs tokens. So

19
00:00:44.953 --> 00:00:47.890
you set max steps: a hard stop.

20
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.330
Add a token budget as well, so one

21
00:00:50.376 --> 00:00:52.327
bad run can't drain your credits.

22
00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:55.661
And when a tool fails, don't crash. Send

23
00:00:55.707 --> 00:00:57.797
the error back as an observation, and the

24
00:00:57.832 --> 00:00:59.829
model usually corrects itself.

25
00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:02.838
That message list is the agent's only memory.

26
00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:05.322
Your code resends all of it on every

27
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.120
turn, so keep tool results short.

28
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.351
So an agent is just a model, some

29
00:01:10.397 --> 00:01:12.243
tools, and a loop that always knows when

30
00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:13.439
to stop.

31
00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:16.854
Next lesson: guardrails, before your agent sends a

32
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.061
single email.
